WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.944 --> 00:00:03.592
- [Narrator] In southern central Bosnia,

00:00:03.592 --> 00:00:05.831
just outside the town of Konjic

00:00:05.831 --> 00:00:08.978
and behind a quiet unassuming
building in the mountains

00:00:08.978 --> 00:00:11.094
lies a secret place,

00:00:11.094 --> 00:00:14.624
a place designed to survive
a nuclear apocalypse.

00:00:14.624 --> 00:00:17.035
Welcome to Tito's Bunker.

00:00:17.035 --> 00:00:20.452
(light mysterious music)

00:00:21.792 --> 00:00:25.621
Construction of the bunker was
started by Josip Broz Tito,

00:00:25.621 --> 00:00:28.985
the president of Yugoslavia
at the height of the Cold War.

00:00:28.985 --> 00:00:31.096
It took 26 years to complete

00:00:31.096 --> 00:00:34.672
and was a well-kept
top secret for decades.

00:00:34.672 --> 00:00:37.525
The horseshoe-shaped structure
goes over 600 feet deep

00:00:37.525 --> 00:00:40.228
into the mountain and
is a maze of offices,

00:00:40.228 --> 00:00:42.212
conferences rooms, doors,

00:00:42.212 --> 00:00:45.640
as well as living quarters
for Tito and his wife.

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:47.507
In the event of a nuclear strike,

00:00:47.507 --> 00:00:51.439
the bunker could protect 350
of the most important political

00:00:51.439 --> 00:00:54.207
and military persons in the country.

00:00:54.207 --> 00:00:56.558
The bunker was almost
destroyed in the early '90s

00:00:56.558 --> 00:00:59.462
during the Bosnian War,
but went untouched,

00:00:59.462 --> 00:01:01.869
remaining a time capsule
from the Cold War,

00:01:01.869 --> 00:01:04.675
its bedrooms, bathrooms,
phones, and typewriters

00:01:04.675 --> 00:01:07.777
still lying ready for atomic war.

00:01:07.777 --> 00:01:10.366
Today, the bunker serves
a more peaceful purpose

00:01:10.366 --> 00:01:13.638
as a modern art museum, housing
one of the most important

00:01:13.638 --> 00:01:17.335
and valuable art collections
in southern Europe.

00:01:17.335 --> 00:01:19.519
Built for war between East and West,

00:01:19.519 --> 00:01:22.202
Tito's Bunker is now a safe
haven for creative works

00:01:22.202 --> 00:01:25.119
from artists from around the world.

